<title>USA: Lawson Products Inc Q4 net, sales rise.</title>
<headline>Lawson Products Inc Q4 net, sales rise.</headline>
<dateline>DES PLAINES, Ill. 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr		     $   0.56		  $  0.49</p>
<p> Net			  6,414		    5,727</p>
<p> Sales		     64,399		   56,420</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  11,457		   11,742</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)  </p>
<p>	  12 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr			$  1.73		  $  1.75</p>
<p> Net			 19,995		   21,120</p>
<p> Sales		    250,289		  223,537</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  11,563		   12,073</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Inventories and cost of goods sold during interim periods are determined through the use of estimated gross profit rates. The difference between actual and estimated gross profit rates used for the interim periods is adjusted in the fourth quarter. This adjustment increased 1996 net by about $528,000 and reduced 1995 net by about $354,000.</p>
<p>	     ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8787))</p>
</text>
